{
  "_readme": "LocalAI Studio optional SKU profile definitions. Each entry describes one hardware class (cloud VM, bare-metal workstation, etc.). Required fields: name (unique display name used in the SKU filter), vram_gb (GPU VRAM in GiB, 0 for CPU-only). Optional fields: vm_size_pattern (cloud VM size string or pattern with # = one digit, ? = one character, * = any characters; accepts a list of patterns too), cpu (CPU/vCPU count), ram_gb, gpu_fraction (human-readable GPU share, e.g. '1/6 GPU'), bench_quick_models / bench_extended_models (per-SKU benchmark default-tick model lists with optional {inherit, add, remove} against bench_defaults.baselines), recommended_models (model ids surfaced as 'Recommended for: <SKU>' badges on the Models page and used to auto-tick the Recommended preset in Benchmark and Image Gen). SKUs must be listed in ascending capability order. Reload via Settings > Reload SKUs (no restart). This file is the SINGLE source of truth for SKU display names and SKU->model recommendations — the app must never hardcode them. Legacy field names azure_size and vcpu are still accepted by the loader for back-compat.",
